# Chezmoi Sync Reminder

When you have finished modifying any Cursor skill, rule, hook script, or MCP config file in this session, remind the user:

> **Dotfiles sync needed.** You changed a managed file. Run this to push to your backup repo:
> ```
> chezmoi add ~/.cursor/skills ~/Documents/work/automation/.cursor/rules ~/.cursor/hooks ~/.cursor/hooks.json ~/.cursorrules && chezmoi git -- add -A && chezmoi git -- commit -m "sync" && chezmoi git -- push
> ```

**Important:** Use `chezmoi add <paths>`, NOT `chezmoi re-add`. `re-add` only re-syncs files chezmoi already tracks -- it silently skips brand-new skills/rules (this is how files have gone missing from the backup before). `chezmoi add` on a directory catches both new and modified files. If a new symlinked skill was added under `~/.cursor/skills/`, `chezmoi add` will prompt about removing the template attribute -- skip symlinks and add their real targets instead, or ask the user.

## When to remind

- After creating or editing any file under `~/.cursor/skills/`
- After creating or editing any `.mdc` file under `~/Documents/work/automation/.cursor/rules/`
- After editing `~/.cursor/hooks.json` or scripts in `~/.cursor/hooks/`
- After editing `~/.cursorrules`
- After editing `~/.cursor/mcp.json` (also remind to update `secrets.yaml` if a token changed)

## When NOT to remind

- If the user already ran the sync command in this session
- If the change was trivial (typo fix) and user said "don't sync"
- During read-only investigations (no file was actually modified)

## Reminder format

Keep it brief -- one line + the command. Do not explain chezmoi or the backup system unless asked. The user already knows.
